        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 意思",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "意思 — yìsi — \"meaning; what something means\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "这个字是什么意思 zhège zì shì shénme yìsi — What does this character mean?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 思 (sī) — nine strokes in two pieces: on top a box with a cross inside it, five strokes; under it 心 xīn, the heart, four strokes. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "意思 (yìsi) is built from 意 'intent' and 思 (sī) 'to think', both inherited from Middle Chinese, 'iH and si (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'will' and the second 'to think of'. The second is said light here."
            }
          ]
        },
